md`# brain-dashboard

A Cloud Brain recipe: metrics read from the lines this Brain's Workers already log. A metric is a definition that names a Worker, the \`at\` of its lines, a numeric field to add up (or none: the lines are counted) and the fields a query may group or filter by. Nothing is added to the Worker that writes the lines. The metrics of the Brain's own Workers are a value of this module; a member's are rows of this service. Tasks 1 and 2 of \`plan/cloud-brain-dashboard-service.md\`; dashboards and the memory of an answer are later tasks and are not here.

| Method | Answers |
|---|---|
| \`GET metric.list\` | \`{ metrics }\`: the definitions the caller may name, no data |
| \`GET metric.query?metric=NAME&since=MS&until=MS&by=dim,dim&DIM=value\` | \`{ metric, since, until, step, groups, series }\`: one Cloudflare telemetry query (\`POST /accounts/ACCOUNT/workers/observability/telemetry/query\`, \`view: "calculations"\`) |
| \`POST metric.put\` | a member's own. Body \`{ name, worker, at, value, dims }\`; answers \`{ metric }\`, the definition as kept. A name that is kept is written over |
| \`POST metric.delete\` | a member's own. Body \`{ name }\`; answers \`{ deleted }\`, or 404 for a name that is not kept |
| Storage | \`rows\`, key \`metric/<name>\`: a member's definition, \`{ name, worker, at, value, dims }\`. The member's DID is not kept |

## The metrics

The metrics of the Brain's own Workers are a value of this module (\`metricDefinitions\`) and no method writes one: adding one is a change to the seed.

| Name | Worker | Lines | Value | Dimensions |
|---|---|---|---|---|
${metricTable}

For a line of the deployer the Worker deployed is \`target\`; \`worker\` on it is the writer. The core's line also holds \`caller\`, \`holder\`, \`delegation\` and \`by\`, which are not dimensions and cannot be asked for.

## A query

\`since\` and \`until\` are times in milliseconds, \`since\` before \`until\`; with neither, the hour before now, and with \`until\` alone the hour before it (an \`until\` under an hour is 400). \`by\` is a list of dimensions of the metric, joined with commas. Any other parameter is a filter and its name is a dimension: \`target=brain-x-git\`, \`status=502\`. A name that is not a dimension of the metric is answered 400, in \`by\` or as a filter, and Cloudflare is not asked.

The caller sends no body of Cloudflare's. The service writes it (\`metricBody\`): the script of the definition's Worker (\`logsScope\` of brain-logs, with the Worker named), the line's \`at\`, the filters asked, \`groupBys\` of \`by\` with each dimension's type, a count, and for a metric with a value its sum and max; \`limit\` 500.

\`\`\`js
GET /xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.metric.query?metric=deploys.confirmed&by=target&since=1791676800000&until=1791680400000
{ "metric": "deploys.confirmed", "since": 1791676800000, "until": 1791680400000,
  "step": 60000,       // Cloudflare's result.run.granularity; the service does not choose it
  "groups": 2,         // how many groups Cloudflare answered; 500 or more means it cut the answer
  "series": [{ "t": 1791676860000, "target": "brain-x-git", "n": 2, "sum": null, "max": null }] }
\`\`\`

A row is one step and one group: \`t\` the step's time, the dimensions asked, \`n\` the lines, \`sum\` and \`max\` of the value (\`null\` for a counted metric). Steps with no line have no row. Cloudflare's refusal is answered 502 with its status in the message.

## Who can call

| Method | Rule |
|---|---|
| \`metric.query\` | \`${metricRules.query}\` |
| \`metric.list\` | \`${metricRules.list}\` |
| \`metric.put\` | \`${metricRules.put}\` |
| \`metric.delete\` | \`${metricRules.delete}\` |

So \`core.calls\` is read by the owner in their own tab, as \`logs.query\` is. A token of the owner reads \`deploys.*\`: counts of what \`logs.deploys\` already gives it. The rule reads \`metric\` from the query string, and a call with none is refused for every caller but the owner in their tab. The owner changes the rule with \`rule.put\` and no deploy.

\`metric.list\` does not follow the rule of \`metric.query\`: a token is listed \`core.calls\` and is refused it.

Whatever a rule has become, the service itself answers two kinds of caller and no other (\`metricTenant\`): the owner, with their tokens, and a member, a caller whose name starts \`did:\`. A Worker, a member's Worker included, and a stranger are answered 403 by every method.

## A member's metrics

A member's metric is named \`m.ID.NAME\` and is over a Worker \`brain-m-ID-SERVICE\`, where \`ID\` is the first ten hex digits of the SHA-256 of the member's DID (\`id\` of \`member.whoami\`; the same id as in the name of their Workers and their repositories). The service computes it from the caller on each call, and nothing a member sends changes it.

\`\`\`js
POST /xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.metric.put
{ "name": "m.0123456789.errors",          // m.ID. and then 1 to 30 of a-z, 0-9 and -
  "worker": "brain-m-0123456789-todo",    // brain-m-ID- and then the service's name, 1 to 20 of a-z and 0-9
  "at": "todo.error",                     // the \`at\` of the lines, 1 to 100 characters
  "value": null,                          // a field of the line that is a number, or null: the lines are counted
  "dims": [{ "key": "kind" }, { "key": "code", "type": "number" }] }   // 8 at most
\`\`\`

A field's name, in \`value\` and in a \`key\`, is a letter or \`_\` and then up to 63 letters, digits, \`_\` and \`.\`. A \`key\` is not \`metric\`, \`since\`, \`until\` or \`by\`, which are parameters of a query. A member keeps ${metricLimits.kept} metrics.

| A member's call | Answer |
|---|---|
| \`metric.put\` with a \`name\` that does not start \`m.ID.\` with their own id, or a \`worker\` that does not start \`brain-m-ID-\` with it | 403 |
| \`metric.put\` with their own name and Worker and a definition that is not one, or a new name when ${metricLimits.kept} are kept | 400 |
| \`metric.delete\` of a name that does not start \`m.ID.\` with their own id | 403 |
| \`metric.query\` of a metric that does not start \`m.ID.\` with their own id: another member's, and every metric of the Brain's own Workers | 403, the same for a name that is kept and one that is not |
| \`metric.query\` of their own name that is not kept | 404 |
| \`metric.list\` | their own definitions and no other |

The owner and their tokens are listed every definition, and are refused \`metric.put\` and \`metric.delete\` by the service (403): a metric written by the owner over a Worker of the Brain would give a token that Worker's lines under another name. The owner in their own tab reads a member's metric with \`metric.query\`, as they read every line with \`logs.query\`; a token does not, by the rule.

What holds one member's counts from another: the script Cloudflare is asked for is the \`worker\` of the definition, a definition is kept only with a \`worker\` of the member who put it, and it is read only by that member's own name. A kept row whose \`worker\` is not its member's (no method writes one) is answered 500 and Cloudflare is not asked.

**A member reaches these methods only when the owner granted them** (\`grant.put\` of each of the four for that DID): the kernel refuses a DID any method outside its own list before a rule is read.

**No price.** Each \`metric.query\` is one query of Cloudflare's logs on the owner's account, and no method here has a price. What one such query costs was not found: Cloudflare prices Workers Logs by the lines written, and says a price for observability starts 2026-12-01 without giving it (read 2026-10-11, \`plan/cloud-brain-dashboard-service.md\`, "Read"). The core counts a member's Worker's calls for a day; a member's own call of a granted method was not found to be counted. What bounds a member today is the grant, which the owner takes back. The owner sets a price with no deploy: \`price.put { target: "com.lopecode.brain.metric.query", price: 'caller.kind == "did" ? 0.001 : 0.0' }\` would charge the account of a member's call a tenth of a cent a query (read in brain-core, \`priced\`, and not run; the number is an example, not a measure).

## The Cloudflare token

The service declares \`cloudflare: ["Workers Observability Read"]\`, as brain-logs does. The deployer mints a token with that one permission and binds it to this Worker alone. It reads the logs of every Worker on the Cloudflare account, which is why a caller's text reaches Cloudflare only as the value of a filter on a dimension the definition names, and the script and \`at\` are the definition's.

## Not known

A member's call on a running Brain: every answer above is from the tests of this module, with the caller's name given to the service as the core gives it. Whether Cloudflare samples a \`calculations\` answer over a long span, as it does a wide \`events\` query (brain-logs, "Whole, not sampled"). What Cloudflare answers for a span that starts before the 7 days it keeps. The shape of an answer with no \`by\`: the service reads a group with no \`groups\` as one row a step.`
// %%
// The metrics of the Brain's own Workers. A value of the seed: no method writes one (plan/cloud-brain-dashboard-service.md, "Two kinds").
metricDefinitions = [
  { name: "core.calls", worker: "brain-core", at: "call", value: "ms", dims: [{ key: "worker" }, { key: "method" }, { key: "status", type: "number" }] },
  { name: "deploys.confirmed", worker: "brain-deployer", at: "deploy.confirmed", value: null, dims: [{ key: "target" }] },
  { name: "deploys.put-back", worker: "brain-deployer", at: "deploy.put-back", value: null, dims: [{ key: "target" }] },
  { name: "deploys.failed", worker: "brain-deployer", at: "deploy.failed", value: null, dims: [{ key: "target" }] }
]
// %%
// The definitions as rows of the reference's table. A cell of its own: a prose cell with a template inside a hole
// is not read as prose at the emit, and the Worker then serves a reference without it.
metricTable = {
  const code = (text) => "`" + text + "`";
  return metricDefinitions.map((d) => `| ${code(d.name)} | ${code(d.worker)} | ${code(`at: "${d.at}"`)} | ${d.value ? code(d.value) + ", summed, and its max" : "none: counted"} | ${d.dims.map((x) => code(x.key) + (x.type === "number" ? " (a number)" : "")).join(", ")} |`).join("\n");
}
// %%
// The rules, read by the service's manifest and by the reference above.
metricRules = ({
  query: 'caller.session || (caller.id == "owner" && request.params.metric.startsWith("deploys.")) || (caller.kind == "did" && request.params.metric.startsWith("m."))',
  list: 'caller.session || caller.id == "owner" || caller.kind == "did"',
  put: 'caller.kind == "did"',
  delete: 'caller.kind == "did"'
})
// %%
metricLimits = ({ kept: 50 })
// %%
// Who a caller is to this service, whatever a rule passed: { id: "" } the owner and their tokens, { id } a member
// (the 10 hex of the SHA-256 of the DID that brain-deployer and brain-git name a member's things by), null anyone else.
metricTenant = async (caller) => (caller === "owner" ? { id: "" } : /^did:/.test(caller || "") ? { id: (await sha256(caller)).slice(0, 10) } : null)
// %%
// The body of a member's metric.put as the definition that is kept: { def }, or { status, error }.
// 403 for a name or a Worker that is not this member's, 400 for a definition that is not one.
metricOwn = (id, body) => {
  const b = body && typeof body === "object" ? body : {};
  const name = "m." + id + ".", worker = "brain-m-" + id + "-", field = /^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_.]{0,63}$/;
  if (typeof b.name !== "string" || !b.name.startsWith(name)) return { status: 403, error: `a member's metric is named ${name}NAME` };
  if (typeof b.worker !== "string" || !b.worker.startsWith(worker)) return { status: 403, error: `a member's metric is over a Worker of their own, ${worker}SERVICE` };
  if (!/^[a-z0-9-]{1,30}$/.test(b.name.slice(name.length))) return { status: 400, error: `name is ${name} and then 1 to 30 of a-z, 0-9 and -` };
  if (!/^[a-z0-9]{1,20}$/.test(b.worker.slice(worker.length))) return { status: 400, error: `worker is ${worker} and then the service's name, 1 to 20 of a-z and 0-9` };
  if (typeof b.at !== "string" || b.at.length < 1 || b.at.length > 100) return { status: 400, error: "at is the `at` of the lines, 1 to 100 characters" };
  if (!(b.value == null || (typeof b.value === "string" && field.test(b.value)))) return { status: 400, error: "value is a field of the line that is a number, or null: the lines are counted" };
  const dims = b.dims == null ? [] : b.dims;
  const ok = (d) => d && typeof d === "object" && typeof d.key === "string" && field.test(d.key) && !["metric", "since", "until", "by"].includes(d.key) && (d.type == null || d.type === "string" || d.type === "number");
  if (!Array.isArray(dims) || dims.length > 8 || !dims.every(ok) || new Set(dims.map((d) => d.key)).size !== dims.length) return { status: 400, error: 'dims is 8 at most of { key } or { key, type: "number" }, each key once; a key is a field of the line and not metric, since, until or by' };
  return { def: { name: b.name, worker: b.worker, at: b.at, value: b.value == null ? null : b.value, dims: dims.map((d) => (d.type === "number" ? { key: d.key, type: "number" } : { key: d.key })) } };
}
// %%
// What a caller asked of one metric, from the query string: { since, until, by, where }, or { error } for a 400.
// A name in `by` or a filter that is not a dimension of the definition is an error, never dropped.
metricAsk = (def, params, now) => {
  const given = (name, or) => (params.has(name) ? (/^\d{1,15}$/.test(params.get(name)) ? Number(params.get(name)) : NaN) : or);
  const until = given("until", now), since = given("since", until - 3600000);
  if (!(since >= 0 && since < until)) return { error: "since and until are times in milliseconds, since before until" };
  const dims = new Map(def.dims.map((d) => [d.key, d.type || "string"]));
  const names = `the dimensions of ${def.name} are ${[...dims.keys()].join(", ")}`;
  const by = (params.get("by") || "").split(",").filter((k) => k !== "");
  if (by.some((k) => !dims.has(k)) || new Set(by).size !== by.length) return { error: "by is a list of dimensions, each once: " + names };
  const where = [];
  for (const [key, value] of params) {
    if (["metric", "since", "until", "by"].includes(key)) continue;
    if (!dims.has(key)) return { error: `${key} is not a parameter or a dimension: ` + names };
    const type = dims.get(key);
    if (type === "number" && !/^-?\d{1,15}$/.test(value)) return { error: `${key} is a whole number` };
    where.push({ key, operation: "eq", type, value: type === "number" ? Number(value) : value });
  }
  return { since, until, by, where };
}
// %%
// Cloudflare's telemetry query for one ask of one definition, inside the script of the definition's Worker.
metricBody = (def, ask, base) => {
  const dims = new Map(def.dims.map((d) => [d.key, d.type || "string"]));
  return logsScope({
    queryId: "metric " + def.name,
    timeframe: { from: ask.since, to: ask.until },
    view: "calculations",
    parameters: {
      calculations: [{ operator: "count" }, ...(def.value ? [{ operator: "sum", key: def.value, keyType: "number" }, { operator: "max", key: def.value, keyType: "number" }] : [])],
      groupBys: ask.by.map((key) => ({ type: dims.get(key), value: key })),
      filters: [{ key: "at", operation: "eq", type: "string", value: def.at }, ...ask.where],
      limit: 500
    }
  }, "query", base, def.worker);
}
// %%
// Cloudflare's `result` as rows { t, …the dimensions asked, n, sum, max }, one a step and group, oldest first.
metricSeries = (result, def, by) => {
  const calcs = (result && result.calculations) || [];
  const of = (name) => calcs.find((c) => String(c.calculation).toLowerCase().startsWith(name)) || { series: [], aggregates: [] };
  const dims = new Map(def.dims.map((d) => [d.key, d.type || "string"]));
  const rows = new Map();
  const field = (name, key) => {
    for (const point of of(name).series || [])
      for (const g of point.data || []) {
        const t = Date.parse(String(point.time).replace(" ", "T") + "Z");
        const values = by.map((k) => ((g.groups || []).find((x) => x.key === k) || {}).value);
        const id = JSON.stringify([t, values]);
        if (!rows.has(id)) rows.set(id, { t, ...Object.fromEntries(by.map((k, i) => [k, dims.get(k) === "number" ? Number(values[i]) : String(values[i])])), n: 0, sum: def.value ? 0 : null, max: def.value ? 0 : null });
        rows.get(id)[key] = Number(g.value) || 0;
      }
  };
  field("count", "n");
  if (def.value) field("sum", "sum"), field("max", "max");
  return { step: ((result && result.run) || {}).granularity || 60000, groups: (of("count").aggregates || []).length, series: [...rows.values()].filter((r) => r.n > 0).sort((a, b) => a.t - b.t) };
}
// %%
dashboard_service = cloudflare.Service(
  "dashboard",
  async (request, { caller }) => {
    const json = (status, body) => new Response(JSON.stringify(body), { status, headers: { "content-type": "application/json" } });
    const refuse = (status, error, message) => json(status, { error, message });
    const url = new URL(request.url), what = url.pathname.split("com.lopecode.brain.").pop();
    const verbs = { "metric.list": "GET", "metric.query": "GET", "metric.put": "POST", "metric.delete": "POST" };
    if (verbs[what] !== request.method) return refuse(404, "MethodNotImplemented", "GET metric.list, GET metric.query, POST metric.put, POST metric.delete");
    // The tenant is held here, whatever a method's rule has become: a member reaches m.<their id>.… and nothing else.
    const who = await metricTenant(caller);
    if (!who) return refuse(403, "Forbidden", "metrics are for the owner and for a member");
    const mine = who.id ? "m." + who.id + "." : null;
    const kept = async (prefix) => (await rows.list("metric/" + prefix)).map((r) => r.value);
    if (what === "metric.list") return json(200, { metrics: mine ? await kept(mine) : [...metricDefinitions, ...(await kept("m."))] });
    if (what === "metric.put" || what === "metric.delete") {
      if (!mine) return refuse(403, "Forbidden", "a member writes their own metrics; a metric of the Brain's own Workers is a value of the seed");
      const body = await request.json().catch(() => null);
      if (what === "metric.put") {
        const own = metricOwn(who.id, body);
        if (own.error) return refuse(own.status, own.status === 403 ? "Forbidden" : "InvalidRequest", own.error);
        if (!(await rows.get("metric/" + own.def.name)) && (await kept(mine)).length >= metricLimits.kept) return refuse(400, "InvalidRequest", `a member keeps ${metricLimits.kept} metrics: delete one first`);
        await rows.put("metric/" + own.def.name, own.def);
        return json(200, { metric: own.def });
      }
      const name = body && typeof body.name === "string" ? body.name : "";
      if (!name.startsWith(mine)) return refuse(403, "Forbidden", `a member deletes their own metrics, named ${mine}NAME`);
      if (!(await rows.get("metric/" + name))) return refuse(404, "NotFound", `no metric ${name} is kept`);
      await rows.delete("metric/" + name);
      return json(200, { deleted: name });
    }
    const name = url.searchParams.get("metric") || "";
    if (mine && !name.startsWith(mine)) return refuse(403, "Forbidden", `a member reads their own metrics, named ${mine}NAME`);
    const def = metricDefinitions.find((d) => d.name === name) || (name.startsWith("m.") ? await rows.get("metric/" + name) : null);
    if (!def) return refuse(404, "NotFound", mine ? `no metric ${name} is kept: metric.list names yours` : "metric is one of " + metricDefinitions.map((d) => d.name).join(", ") + ", or a member's (metric.list)");
    // The script Cloudflare is asked for is the tenant: a kept definition is read only over a Worker of the member it is named for.
    if (!metricDefinitions.includes(def) && !String(def.worker).startsWith("brain-m-" + name.split(".")[1] + "-")) return refuse(500, "InternalError", `the kept definition of ${name} is not over a Worker of its member`);
    const ask = metricAsk(def, url.searchParams, Date.now());
    if (ask.error) return refuse(400, "InvalidRequest", ask.error);
    const r = await cloudflareApi.fetch("/workers/observability/telemetry/query", { method: "POST", body: JSON.stringify(metricBody(def, ask, config.base)) });
    const data = await r.json().catch(() => null);
    if (!r.ok || !data || !data.result) return refuse(502, "UpstreamFailure", `Cloudflare answered ${r.status} ${JSON.stringify((data && data.errors) || null).slice(0, 300)}`);
    return json(200, { metric: def.name, since: ask.since, until: ask.until, ...metricSeries(data.result, def, ask.by) });
  },
  {
    cloudflare: ["Workers Observability Read"],
    methods: {
      "com.lopecode.brain.metric.list": { type: "query", allow: metricRules.list },
      "com.lopecode.brain.metric.query": { type: "query", allow: metricRules.query },
      "com.lopecode.brain.metric.put": { type: "procedure", allow: metricRules.put },
      "com.lopecode.brain.metric.delete": { type: "procedure", allow: metricRules.delete }
    }
  }
)
// %%
dashboard_announce = {
  plugins.add("workers", dashboard_service, { invalidation });
  return "announced dashboard_service";
}
// %%
md`## Tests`
// %%
// The service with a stand-in for Cloudflare: `answer(body)` gives the result of one telemetry query, or a Response.
dashboardRig = async (answer = () => ({ run: { granularity: 60000 }, calculations: [] })) => {
  const seen = [];
  const sim = await simulate(dashboard_service, {
    secrets: { CF_TOKEN: "minted-1", BRAIN_KEY: "k" },
    config: { base: "cb4", account: "acct" },
    fetch: async (request) => {
      const body = await request.json();
      seen.push({ url: request.url, authorization: request.headers.get("authorization"), body });
      const out = answer(body);
      return out instanceof Response ? out : new Response(JSON.stringify({ success: true, result: out }), { headers: { "content-type": "application/json" } });
    }
  });
  // A token of the owner unless told: the owner with no tab.
  const token = { "x-brain-caller": "owner", "x-brain-via": "delegation:b6559fa96c36", "x-brain-holder": "secret:loop-dashboard", "x-brain-tab": "0" };
  const call = async (method, query = "", { headers = token, verb = "GET", body = {} } = {}) => {
    const r = await sim.fetch("https://dashboard.internal/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain." + method + query, { method: verb, headers, ...(verb === "GET" ? {} : { body: JSON.stringify(body) }) });
    return { status: r.status, data: await r.json() };
  };
  // A member: their id, and their calls. `write` is a POST with a body, `read` a GET.
  const member = async (did) => {
    const headers = { "x-brain-caller": did }, id = (await sha256(did)).slice(0, 10);
    return { did, id, write: (method, body) => call(method, "", { headers, verb: "POST", body }), read: (method, query = "") => call(method, query, { headers }) };
  };
  return { sim, seen, call, member };
}
// %%
// R1 of the spec: one body, written from the definition and from what was asked as data.
test_metric_query_sends_cloudflare_one_body_written_from_the_definition = {
  const H = 3600000, since = 1791676800000, until = since + H;
  // Cloudflare's shape as cb4 gave it on 2026-10-09 (test_calls_from_the_logs_become_chart_rows of the page): a list a calculation, a row a step and group.
  const group = (pairs, value) => ({ groups: Object.entries(pairs).map(([key, v]) => ({ key, value: v })), groupKey: Object.values(pairs).join(" ⬤ "), value });
  const calc = (calculation, aggregates, at) => ({ calculation, aggregates, series: Object.entries(at).map(([time, data]) => ({ time, data })) });
  const git = { target: "brain-x-git" }, echo = { target: "brain-x-echo" };
  const counted = { run: { granularity: 60000 }, calculations: [calc("count", [group(git, 3), group(echo, 1)], { "2026-10-11 16:01:00": [group(git, 2), group(echo, 1)], "2026-10-11 16:02:00": [group(git, 1)], "2026-10-11 16:03:00": [] })] };
  const rig = await dashboardRig((body) => (body.queryId === "metric core.calls" ? valued : counted));
  const out = await rig.call("metric.query", `?metric=deploys.confirmed&by=target&since=${since}&until=${until}`);
  expect(out.status).toBe(200);
  expect(rig.seen.length).toBe(1);
  expect(rig.seen[0]).toEqual({
    url: "https://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4/accounts/acct/workers/observability/telemetry/query",
    authorization: "Bearer minted-1",
    body: {
      queryId: "metric deploys.confirmed",
      timeframe: { from: since, to: until },
      view: "calculations",
      parameters: {
        datasets: ["cloudflare-workers"],
        filterCombination: "and",
        filters: [{ key: "$workers.scriptName", operation: "eq", type: "string", value: "cb4-deployer" }, { kind: "group", filterCombination: "and", filters: [{ key: "at", operation: "eq", type: "string", value: "deploy.confirmed" }] }],
        calculations: [{ operator: "count" }],
        groupBys: [{ type: "string", value: "target" }],
        limit: 500
      }
    }
  });
  const at = (minute) => Date.UTC(2026, 9, 11, 16, minute);
  expect(out.data).toEqual({ metric: "deploys.confirmed", since, until, step: 60000, groups: 2, series: [{ t: at(1), target: "brain-x-git", n: 2, sum: null, max: null }, { t: at(1), target: "brain-x-echo", n: 1, sum: null, max: null }, { t: at(2), target: "brain-x-git", n: 1, sum: null, max: null }] });
  // A metric with a value: its sum and max are asked, a number dimension is grouped and filtered as a number, and the script is the core's.
  const poll = { worker: "brain-x-inbox", status: 200 }, bad = { worker: "brain-x-inbox", status: 502 };
  const valued = { run: { granularity: 300000 }, calculations: [
    calc("count", [group(poll, 2), group(bad, 1)], { "2026-10-11 16:00:00": [group(poll, 2)], "2026-10-11 16:05:00": [group(bad, 1)] }),
    calc("sum(ms)", [], { "2026-10-11 16:00:00": [group(poll, 80)], "2026-10-11 16:05:00": [group(bad, 900)] }),
    calc("max(ms)", [], { "2026-10-11 16:00:00": [group(poll, 50)], "2026-10-11 16:05:00": [group(bad, 900)] })
  ] };
  const owner = { "x-brain-caller": "owner", "x-brain-via": "session", "x-brain-tab": "1" };
  const calls = await rig.call("metric.query", `?metric=core.calls&by=worker,status&method=inbox.poll&status=200&since=${since}&until=${until}`, { headers: owner });
  expect(rig.seen.length).toBe(2);
  expect(rig.seen[1].body.parameters).toEqual({
    datasets: ["cloudflare-workers"],
    filterCombination: "and",
    filters: [{ key: "$workers.scriptName", operation: "eq", type: "string", value: "cb4-core" }, { kind: "group", filterCombination: "and", filters: [{ key: "at", operation: "eq", type: "string", value: "call" }, { key: "method", operation: "eq", type: "string", value: "inbox.poll" }, { key: "status", operation: "eq", type: "number", value: 200 }] }],
    calculations: [{ operator: "count" }, { operator: "sum", key: "ms", keyType: "number" }, { operator: "max", key: "ms", keyType: "number" }],
    groupBys: [{ type: "string", value: "worker" }, { type: "number", value: "status" }],
    limit: 500
  });
  expect(calls.data).toEqual({ metric: "core.calls", since, until, step: 300000, groups: 2, series: [{ t: at(0), worker: "brain-x-inbox", status: 200, n: 2, sum: 80, max: 50 }, { t: at(5), worker: "brain-x-inbox", status: 502, n: 1, sum: 900, max: 900 }] });
  // With no span, the hour before now; with no `by`, no groupBys and one row a step.
  const whole = await dashboardRig(() => ({ run: { granularity: 60000 }, calculations: [calc("count", [{ value: 4 }], { "2026-10-11 16:01:00": [{ value: 4 }] })] }));
  const now = await whole.call("metric.query", "?metric=deploys.failed");
  expect(now.data.until - now.data.since).toBe(H);
  expect(Math.abs(now.data.until - Date.now())).toBeLessThan(600000);
  expect(whole.seen[0].body.parameters.groupBys).toEqual([]);
  expect(now.data.series).toEqual([{ t: at(1), n: 4, sum: null, max: null }]);
  return "3 bodies";
}
// %%
// R3 of the spec: the rule on the method reads the metric's name.
test_metric_rules_give_a_token_the_deploy_counts_and_the_owners_tab_the_rest = {
  const { meta } = await dashboard_service.emit();
  // The five callers of brain-logs' rule test: the owner in a tab, a token of the owner, a member, a Worker, a stranger.
  const callers = [{ caller: "owner", via: "session", tab: true }, { caller: "owner", via: "delegation:b6559fa96c36", holder: "secret:loop-dashboard", tab: false }, { caller: "did:plc:member" }, { caller: "worker:brain-x-echo" }, { caller: "anonymous" }];
  const may = (nsid, params) => callers.map((who) => decide({ allow: meta.access[nsid].allow }, { caller: callerOf(who), origin: callerOf(who), request: { params } }).allow);
  const query = "com.lopecode.brain.metric.query", list = "com.lopecode.brain.metric.list", put = "com.lopecode.brain.metric.put", del = "com.lopecode.brain.metric.delete";
  expect(Object.entries(meta.access).map(([nsid, a]) => [nsid, a.type, a.allow])).toEqual([[del, "procedure", metricRules.delete], [list, "query", metricRules.list], [put, "procedure", metricRules.put], [query, "query", metricRules.query]]);
  // A write is a member's: not the owner in a tab, not a token.
  expect(may(put, {})).toEqual([false, false, true, false, false]);
  expect(may(del, {})).toEqual([false, false, true, false, false]);
  expect([meta.access[query].price, meta.access[put].price]).toEqual([undefined, undefined]);
  expect(may(query, { metric: "core.calls" })).toEqual([true, false, false, false, false]);
  expect(may(query, { metric: "deploys.confirmed" })).toEqual([true, true, false, false, false]);
  expect(may(query, { metric: "deploys.put-back" })).toEqual([true, true, false, false, false]);
  expect(may(query, { metric: "m.x.y" })).toEqual([true, false, true, false, false]);
  // A name that only holds "deploys." or "m." is not one that starts with it.
  expect(may(query, { metric: "core.deploys.x" })).toEqual([true, false, false, false, false]);
  expect(may(query, { metric: "xm.deploys." })).toEqual([true, false, false, false, false]);
  // With no metric the rule cannot be read: everyone but the owner in their tab is refused.
  expect(may(query, {})).toEqual([true, false, false, false, false]);
  expect(may(list, {})).toEqual([true, true, true, false, false]);
  return "10 rows of 5 callers";
}
// %%
// R3 of the spec: what the definition does not name is refused before Cloudflare is asked, and no method writes a definition.
test_metric_query_refuses_what_the_definition_does_not_name = {
  const since = 1791676800000, until = since + 3600000, span = `&since=${since}&until=${until}`;
  const rig = await dashboardRig();
  const owner = { headers: { "x-brain-caller": "owner", "x-brain-via": "session", "x-brain-tab": "1" } };
  const status = async (method, query, options) => [query, (await rig.call(method, query, options)).status];
  // The core's line names who called. None of that is a dimension, in `by` or as a filter; nor is a dimension of another metric.
  for (const bad of ["&by=caller", "&by=worker,caller", "&by=holder", "&by=target", "&caller=owner", "&delegation=x", "&ray=a", "&by=worker,worker", "&status=2xx", "&status=200%20or%201", "&filters=x", "&worker=a&at=deploy.reason"])
    expect(await status("metric.query", "?metric=core.calls" + span + bad, owner)).toEqual(["?metric=core.calls" + span + bad, 400]);
  expect(await status("metric.query", "?metric=deploys.confirmed&by=worker" + span)).toEqual(["?metric=deploys.confirmed&by=worker" + span, 400]);
  // A span that is not one.
  // `until` alone under an hour would send Cloudflare a time before 1970 (a note of review 1502).
  for (const bad of [`&since=${until}&until=${since}`, `&since=${since}&until=${since}`, "&since=yesterday", `&since=${since}&until=`, "&since=-5", "&until=5", "&until=3599999"])
    expect(await status("metric.query", "?metric=deploys.confirmed" + bad)).toEqual(["?metric=deploys.confirmed" + bad, 400]);
  // A metric that is not defined, and no metric.
  for (const none of ["?metric=deploys.reason", "?metric=m.x.y", "?metric=", "", "?metric=core.calls%20"]) expect(await status("metric.query", none + (none ? span : ""), owner)).toEqual([none + (none ? span : ""), 404]);
  // No method writes a definition for the owner: a read is a GET, a write is a member's (403), and there is no other method.
  for (const [method, verb, status] of [["metric.put", "POST", 403], ["metric.delete", "POST", 403], ["metric.put", "GET", 404], ["metric.delete", "GET", 404], ["metric.query", "POST", 404], ["metric.list", "POST", 404], ["dashboard.put", "POST", 404], ["logs.query", "POST", 404]])
    expect([method, verb, (await rig.call(method, "?metric=x.y", { ...owner, verb, body: { name: "core.mine", worker: "brain-core", at: "call", value: null, dims: [{ key: "caller" }] } })).status]).toEqual([method, verb, status]);
  expect(rig.sim.rows.size).toBe(0);
  expect((await rig.call("metric.list", "", owner)).data).toEqual({ metrics: metricDefinitions });
  expect(metricDefinitions.map((d) => d.name)).toEqual(["core.calls", "deploys.confirmed", "deploys.put-back", "deploys.failed"]);
  // A member with no metric of their own: no definition, and no data of any metric.
  const member = { headers: { "x-brain-caller": "did:plc:alicemember" } };
  expect(await rig.call("metric.list", "", member)).toEqual({ status: 200, data: { metrics: [] } });
  for (const name of ["deploys.confirmed", "core.calls", "m.x.y", ""]) expect(await status("metric.query", "?metric=" + name + span, member)).toEqual(["?metric=" + name + span, 403]);
  // Nothing above reached Cloudflare.
  expect(rig.seen.length).toBe(0);
  // Cloudflare's refusal is an error of this method, with its status named.
  const down = await dashboardRig(() => new Response('{"success":false,"errors":[{"code":10000,"message":"rate limited"}]}', { status: 429, headers: { "content-type": "application/json" } }));
  const out = await down.call("metric.query", "?metric=deploys.confirmed" + span);
  expect([out.status, out.data.error]).toEqual([502, "UpstreamFailure"]);
  expect(out.data.message).toContain("429");
  return "nothing sent to Cloudflare";
}
// %%
// R6 of the spec, the metric half: a member writes, lists, reads and deletes metrics over their own Workers, and no other's.
test_a_member_keeps_and_reads_metrics_of_their_own_workers_and_no_others = {
  const since = 1791676800000, until = since + 3600000, span = `&since=${since}&until=${until}`;
  const rig = await dashboardRig();
  const alice = await rig.member("did:plc:alice"), bob = await rig.member("did:plc:bob");
  const errors = (m, worker = "todo") => ({ name: `m.${m.id}.errors`, worker: `brain-m-${m.id}-${worker}`, at: "todo.error", value: null, dims: [{ key: "kind" }, { key: "code", type: "number" }] });
  // Over another member's Worker: refused, under either name. Over their own: kept, as the definition a built-in one is.
  expect((await alice.write("metric.put", { ...errors(alice), worker: `brain-m-${bob.id}-todo` })).status).toBe(403);
  expect((await alice.write("metric.put", { ...errors(bob), worker: `brain-m-${alice.id}-todo` })).status).toBe(403);
  expect((await alice.write("metric.put", errors(bob))).status).toBe(403);
  expect(rig.sim.rows.size).toBe(0);
  expect(await alice.write("metric.put", errors(alice))).toEqual({ status: 200, data: { metric: errors(alice) } });
  expect((await alice.write("metric.put", { name: `m.${alice.id}.slow`, worker: `brain-m-${alice.id}-todo`, at: "todo.done", value: "ms" })).data).toEqual({ metric: { name: `m.${alice.id}.slow`, worker: `brain-m-${alice.id}-todo`, at: "todo.done", value: "ms", dims: [] } });
  expect((await bob.write("metric.put", errors(bob, "shop"))).status).toBe(200);
  expect([...rig.sim.rows.keys()].sort()).toEqual([`metric/m.${alice.id}.errors`, `metric/m.${alice.id}.slow`, `metric/m.${bob.id}.errors`].sort());
  expect(rig.sim.rows.get(`metric/m.${alice.id}.errors`)).toEqual(errors(alice));
  // The Brain's own Workers, a Worker that is not a member's, a name of the Brain's metrics: none is a member's to write.
  for (const body of [{ ...errors(alice), worker: "brain-core" }, { ...errors(alice), worker: "brain-x-git" }, { ...errors(alice), worker: `brain-m-${alice.id}` }, { ...errors(alice), name: "deploys.mine" }, { ...errors(alice), name: "core.calls" }, { ...errors(alice), name: `m.${alice.id}` }, { ...errors(alice), name: `m.${alice.id.toUpperCase()}.x` }, {}, null, "m"])
    expect([JSON.stringify(body), (await alice.write("metric.put", body)).status]).toEqual([JSON.stringify(body), 403]);
  // A definition that is not one: 400.
  const nine = Array.from({ length: 9 }, (_, i) => ({ key: "d" + i }));
  for (const change of [{ name: `m.${alice.id}.` }, { name: `m.${alice.id}.A` }, { name: `m.${alice.id}.a.b` }, { name: `m.${alice.id}.${"a".repeat(31)}` }, { worker: `brain-m-${alice.id}-` }, { worker: `brain-m-${alice.id}-to-do` }, { worker: `brain-m-${alice.id}-${"a".repeat(21)}` }, { at: "" }, { at: 5 }, { at: "a".repeat(101) }, { value: 5 }, { value: "$workers.scriptName" }, { value: "a b" }, { dims: nine }, { dims: "kind" }, { dims: [{ key: "kind" }, { key: "kind" }] }, { dims: [{ key: "by" }] }, { dims: [{ key: "since" }] }, { dims: [{ key: "metric" }] }, { dims: [{ key: "$metadata.id" }] }, { dims: [{ key: "kind", type: "date" }] }, { dims: [null] }, { dims: ["kind"] }])
    expect([JSON.stringify(change).slice(0, 60), (await alice.write("metric.put", { ...errors(alice), ...change })).status]).toEqual([JSON.stringify(change).slice(0, 60), 400]);
  expect(rig.sim.rows.size).toBe(3);
  // The list: a member their own and no other, the owner and their tokens every definition.
  expect((await alice.read("metric.list")).data.metrics.map((d) => d.name)).toEqual([`m.${alice.id}.errors`, `m.${alice.id}.slow`]);
  expect((await bob.read("metric.list")).data).toEqual({ metrics: [errors(bob, "shop")] });
  expect((await rig.call("metric.list")).data.metrics.map((d) => d.name).sort()).toEqual([...metricDefinitions.map((d) => d.name), `m.${alice.id}.errors`, `m.${alice.id}.slow`, `m.${bob.id}.errors`].sort());
  // A read: their own is one body to Cloudflare inside the script of their own Worker. Another member's, and every built-in one, is 403.
  expect(rig.seen.length).toBe(0);
  const own = await alice.read("metric.query", `?metric=m.${alice.id}.errors&by=kind&code=500` + span);
  expect([own.status, own.data.metric, own.data.series]).toEqual([200, `m.${alice.id}.errors`, []]);
  expect(rig.seen.length).toBe(1);
  expect(rig.seen[0].body.parameters).toEqual({
    datasets: ["cloudflare-workers"],
    filterCombination: "and",
    filters: [{ key: "$workers.scriptName", operation: "eq", type: "string", value: `cb4-m-${alice.id}-todo` }, { kind: "group", filterCombination: "and", filters: [{ key: "at", operation: "eq", type: "string", value: "todo.error" }, { key: "code", operation: "eq", type: "number", value: 500 }] }],
    calculations: [{ operator: "count" }],
    groupBys: [{ type: "string", value: "kind" }],
    limit: 500
  });
  for (const name of [`m.${bob.id}.errors`, `m.${bob.id}.none`, "deploys.confirmed", "deploys.put-back", "core.calls", "m.", "m", "", `M.${alice.id}.errors`, `xm.${alice.id}.errors`])
    expect([name, (await alice.read("metric.query", "?metric=" + name + span)).status]).toEqual([name, 403]);
  expect((await alice.read("metric.query", span.replace("&", "?"))).status).toBe(403);
  expect((await alice.read("metric.query", `?metric=m.${alice.id}.none` + span)).status).toBe(404);
  expect((await alice.read("metric.query", `?metric=m.${alice.id}.errors&by=caller` + span)).status).toBe(400);
  expect(rig.seen.length).toBe(1);
  // The owner in their tab reads a member's metric by its name, as they read every line with logs.query.
  const tab = { headers: { "x-brain-caller": "owner", "x-brain-via": "session", "x-brain-tab": "1" } };
  expect((await rig.call("metric.query", `?metric=m.${bob.id}.errors` + span, tab)).status).toBe(200);
  expect(rig.seen[1].body.parameters.filters[0].value).toBe(`cb4-m-${bob.id}-shop`);
  // A delete: their own. Another member's is 403 and stays.
  expect((await bob.write("metric.delete", { name: `m.${alice.id}.errors` })).status).toBe(403);
  expect((await alice.write("metric.delete", { name: "deploys.confirmed" })).status).toBe(403);
  expect((await alice.write("metric.delete", {})).status).toBe(403);
  expect(rig.sim.rows.size).toBe(3);
  expect(await alice.write("metric.delete", { name: `m.${alice.id}.errors` })).toEqual({ status: 200, data: { deleted: `m.${alice.id}.errors` } });
  expect((await alice.write("metric.delete", { name: `m.${alice.id}.errors` })).status).toBe(404);
  expect((await alice.read("metric.query", `?metric=m.${alice.id}.errors` + span)).status).toBe(404);
  expect([...rig.sim.rows.keys()].sort()).toEqual([`metric/m.${alice.id}.slow`, `metric/m.${bob.id}.errors`].sort());
  // Who is not a member writes nothing: the owner in their tab, a token, a member's Worker, a stranger, a DID spelled in capitals.
  const callers = [tab.headers, undefined, { "x-brain-caller": `worker:brain-m-${alice.id}-todo` }, { "x-brain-caller": "anonymous" }, {}, { "x-brain-caller": "DID:plc:alice" }, { "x-brain-caller": "deployer" }];
  for (const headers of callers) for (const method of ["metric.put", "metric.delete"])
    expect([JSON.stringify(headers), method, (await rig.call(method, "", { ...(headers ? { headers } : {}), verb: "POST", body: errors(alice) })).status]).toEqual([JSON.stringify(headers), method, 403]);
  // And who is neither the owner nor a member reads nothing, whatever the rule has become.
  for (const headers of callers.slice(2)) for (const [method, query] of [["metric.list", ""], ["metric.query", "?metric=deploys.confirmed" + span], ["metric.query", `?metric=m.${bob.id}.errors` + span]])
    expect([JSON.stringify(headers), method + query, (await rig.call(method, query, { headers })).status]).toEqual([JSON.stringify(headers), method + query, 403]);
  expect(rig.sim.rows.size).toBe(2);
  expect(rig.seen.length).toBe(2);
  // 50 metrics a member: the 51st name is refused, a kept name is still written over.
  for (let i = 0; i < 49; i++) rig.sim.rows.set(`metric/m.${alice.id}.n${i}`, { ...errors(alice), name: `m.${alice.id}.n${i}` });
  expect((await alice.write("metric.put", { ...errors(alice), name: `m.${alice.id}.one-more` })).status).toBe(400);
  expect((await alice.write("metric.put", { ...errors(alice), name: `m.${alice.id}.slow`, at: "todo.slow" })).status).toBe(200);
  expect(rig.sim.rows.get(`metric/m.${alice.id}.slow`).at).toBe("todo.slow");
  expect((await bob.write("metric.put", { ...errors(bob), name: `m.${bob.id}.second` })).status).toBe(200);
  // A row that names a Worker which is not its member's (no method writes one) is not read from Cloudflare.
  rig.sim.rows.set(`metric/m.${alice.id}.n0`, { ...errors(alice), name: `m.${alice.id}.n0`, worker: "brain-core" });
  expect((await alice.read("metric.query", `?metric=m.${alice.id}.n0` + span)).status).toBe(500);
  expect(rig.seen.length).toBe(2);
  return "2 bodies sent to Cloudflare";
}
// %%
test_dashboard_declares_one_cloudflare_permission_and_its_rows = {
  const { meta, parts, source } = await dashboard_service.emit();
  expect(meta.worker).toBe("brain-x-dashboard");
  // The reference the Worker serves holds the first cell with its holes filled: a row a definition, and both rules.
  expect(source.reference.startsWith("# brain-dashboard")).toBe(true);
  for (const d of metricDefinitions) expect(source.reference).toContain("| `" + d.name + "` | `" + d.worker + "` |");
  expect(source.reference).toContain("| `metric.query` | `" + metricRules.query + "` |");
  expect(source.reference).toContain("| `metric.list` | `" + metricRules.list + "` |");
  expect(source.reference).toContain("| `metric.put` | `" + metricRules.put + "` |");
  expect(source.reference).toContain("| `metric.delete` | `" + metricRules.delete + "` |");
  expect(source.reference).toContain("A member keeps " + metricLimits.kept + " metrics.");
  expect(source.reference).not.toMatch(/\$\{/);
  expect(meta.cloudflare).toEqual(["Workers Observability Read"]);
  // Rows for a member's definitions, beside the Cloudflare token: the first service with both.
  expect([meta.resources, meta.secrets, meta.calls]).toEqual([["rows"], [], []]);
  // The token is read from the binding the deployer made, and the script filter is brain-logs' own cell, carried into this Worker.
  expect(parts[0].text).toContain("__rt.platform.secrets.CF_TOKEN");
  expect(parts[0].text).toContain("$workers.scriptName");
  expect(parts[0].text).toMatch(/const logsScope = /);
  expect(parts[0].text).toMatch(/const logsScript = /);
  // Every definition is over a Worker of the Brain, with at most 8 dimensions, none of them who called.
  for (const d of metricDefinitions) {
    expect([d.name, logsScript("cb4", d.worker) !== null, d.dims.length <= 8, /^[a-z]+\.[a-z-]+$/.test(d.name)]).toEqual([d.name, true, true, true]);
    expect(d.dims.map((x) => x.key).filter((k) => ["caller", "holder", "delegation", "by", "origin", "via", "ray", "reason"].includes(k))).toEqual([]);
  }
  return meta.cloudflare[0];
}
// %%
import {cloudflare, cloudflareApi, rows, config, simulate, decide, callerOf, sha256} from "@tomlarkworthy/cloudflare-iac"
// %%
import {logsScope, logsScript} from "@tomlarkworthy/brain-logs"
// %%
import {plugins} from "@tomlarkworthy/plugin-registry"
// %%
import {expect} from "@tomlarkworthy/jest-expect-standalone"
